aquinas-will-antecedent.logic.r2: argue/scope: P5 (S4): read with the necessity on its consequent alone, □((wills → comes) → □(wills → comes)), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, □((wills → comes) → (wills → comes)), C1 (S4) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
aquinas-will-antecedent.logic.r2: argue/scope: P1 (S2): read with the necessity on its consequent alone, □(nec_by_cause → □comes), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, □(nec_by_cause → comes), C (S5) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
